 The following directives are provided for module and class contents:
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option describes the
+   type represented by the alias and is shown in the signature after an equals
+   sign. Its expression is parsed as a Python annotation, so referenced types
+   are cross-referenced normally. A description may be placed in the directive
+   body. As with other non-container Python objects, nested object directives
+   are not allowed.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the module containing the alias. The default is the module
+      specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
